{
	"name": "Leaf Drake",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-fire-breath-orange.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>These Tiny members of dragonkind have jagged, broad wings that run nearly the entire lengths of their slender bodies, giving them the silhouette of a particularly large leaf. The shape that these “leaves” take on vary based on the biome that the leaf drake is found in. But, unlike most dragons, leaf drakes cannot truly fly; instead, they may spread their pseudo-wings and gently glide down from a higher surface (such as a branch) to the ground. Adventurers who spend 1 minute observing leaf drakes drifting on the winds may accurately predict the weather in this region for the next 24 hours.</p><p>Additionally, if an adventurer climbs to a leaf drake’s point of origin, they may discover the tiny dragon’s mighty hoard. Leaf drakes collect shiny objects, such as dropped trinkets and glittering rocks, though any objects hoarded by the drake are of a size that it can feasibly carry—and often of dubious value.</p>",
